      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 2.58,
          "en": "So you did now learn about this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.58,
          "end": 3.86,
          "en": "memoization feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.42,
          "end": 7.14,
          "en": "Now what might be weird though is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.14,
          "end": 10.56,
          "en": "after this one initial request, if I reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.56,
          "end": 12.84,
          "en": "this page or if I go to a different page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.84,
          "end": 16.059,
          "en": "and come back, no further requests are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.059,
          "end": 17.16,
          "en": "sent to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.54,
          "end": 20.36,
          "en": "As you can tell by the fact that no new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.36,
          "end": 22.08,
          "en": "logs are being added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.78,
          "end": 25.7,
          "en": "At least that will be the case if you are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.7,
          "end": 28.18,
          "en": "using Next.js version 14.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28,
          "end": 30.64,
          "en": "And as mentioned before, you can check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.64,
          "end": 32.96,
          "en": "your package.json file to find out which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.96,
          "end": 34.14,
          "en": "version you are using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 34.68,
          "end": 38.54,
          "en": "If you are on Next.js version 15 or higher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.86,
          "end": 42.72,
          "en": "you actually will see multiple requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.72,
          "end": 45.06,
          "en": "here because the default caching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 45.06,
          "end": 48.28,
          "en": "behavior of fetch requests, so of requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.28,
          "end": 50.54,
          "en": "sent with the fetch function as we are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.54,
          "end": 52.7,
          "en": "doing it here, has been changed with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 52.7,
          "end": 54.1,
          "en": "Next.js version 15.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55,
          "end": 56.52,
          "en": "Now I'll get back to that and for the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 56.52,
          "end": 58.3,
          "en": "moment, I'll assume you are using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 58.3,
          "end": 61.44,
          "en": "Next.js version 14 or older, and I'll walk",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 61.44,
          "end": 63.1,
          "en": "you through the behavior there before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 63.1,
          "end": 64.959,
          "en": "I'll then get back to the Next.js version 15",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 64.959,
          "end": 65.4,
          "en": "behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 66.24,
          "end": 69.1,
          "en": "No matter how often I reload this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 69.1,
          "end": 72.62,
          "en": "or navigate back and forth, no new logs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 72.62,
          "end": 73.34,
          "en": "are added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 74.06,
          "end": 77.26,
          "en": "And that's the case because of this data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 77.26,
          "end": 80.36,
          "en": "cache that's also provided by Next.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 81,
          "end": 84.86,
          "en": "Because what Next.js does when using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 84.86,
          "end": 87.7,
          "en": "the fetch function for fetching data from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 87.7,
          "end": 92.75999999999999,
          "en": "a backend is it will store the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 92.75999999999999,
          "end": 95.12,
          "en": "data fetched from there in some",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 95.12,
          "end": 98.06,
          "en": "internally managed server-side cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 98.06,
          "end": 101.58,
          "en": "and it will keep reusing that data forever",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 101.58,
          "end": 105.46000000000001,
          "en": "until you tell it to not do that anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106.02000000000001,
          "end": 109.56,
          "en": "Now, how can you tell Next.js to not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.56,
          "end": 110.97999999999999,
          "en": "reuse that data anymore?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 111.86,
          "end": 117.53999999999999,
          "en": "Well, you could call revalidatePath as you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 117.53999999999999,
          "end": 119.82,
          "en": "learned before in this course after you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 122.24,
          "en": "changed some data, but here I'm not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 122.24,
          "end": 123.98,
          "en": "actually changing the data on that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 123.98,
          "end": 126.16,
          "en": "dummy backend, so I won't do that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 126.32,
          "end": 128.919,
          "en": "but you could do that as you learned it in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 128.919,
          "end": 130.82,
          "en": "the previous section already because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 130.82,
          "end": 134.12,
          "en": "that would tell Next.js that the data for a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 134.12,
          "end": 136.72,
          "en": "specific path, so the data used on a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 136.72,
          "end": 139.14,
          "en": "specific page, did change and it would",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 139.14,
          "end": 141.9,
          "en": "throw away the respective data cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 143.3,
          "end": 146.82,
          "en": "But alternatively, you can also configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 146.82,
          "end": 151.1,
          "en": "this fetch function because you can add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 151.1,
          "end": 154.1,
          "en": "a configuration object to it and on that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 154.1,
          "end": 157.32,
          "en": "configuration object, you can set various",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 157.32,
          "end": 157.92000000000002,
          "en": "settings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 158.44,
          "end": 160.76,
          "en": "For example, the cache setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 161.26,
          "end": 163.57999999999998,
          "en": "You can do that when using fetch in the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 163.57999999999998,
          "end": 165.6,
          "en": "browser side and you can also do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 165.6,
          "end": 167.44,
          "en": "when using fetch on the server side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 168.14,
          "end": 170.12,
          "en": "Now, what's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 170.12,
          "end": 173.76,
          "en": "here is that on the server side, Next.js is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 173.76,
          "end": 177.46,
          "en": "actually overriding the default built-in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 177.46,
          "end": 180,
          "en": "function that is provided by modern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 180,
          "end": 183.52,
          "en": "Node.js and it essentially does that so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 183.52,
          "end": 185.96,
          "en": "that it can find out what cache settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 185.96,
          "end": 188.44,
          "en": "you set up here because that will then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 188.44,
          "end": 190.7,
          "en": "change the behavior of the Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 190.7,
          "end": 191.84,
          "en": "cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 192,
          "end": 194.4,
          "en": "And here, you get various options,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 194.82,
          "end": 197.18,
          "en": "though the two important options when",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 197.18,
          "end": 200.48,
          "en": "using Next.js are force cache, which is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 200.48,
          "end": 203.7,
          "en": "the default with Next.js version 14, which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 203.7,
          "end": 205.7,
          "en": "gives you the most aggressive caching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 205.7,
          "end": 210.12,
          "en": "behavior as this setting, force cache, will",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 210.12,
          "end": 214.52,
          "en": "ensure that the response yielded for this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 214.52,
          "end": 217.56,
          "en": "fetch request will be cached and reused",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 217.56,
          "end": 221.84,
          "en": "across requests until you give Next.js an",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 221.84,
          "end": 224.6,
          "en": "indication that the fetched data has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 224.6,
          "end": 225.12,
          "en": "changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 225.32,
          "end": 227.76,
          "en": "So that's the aggressive default behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 227.76,
          "end": 229.57999999999998,
          "en": "you get with Next.js 14.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 230.02,
          "end": 234.06,
          "en": "The other important setting is no store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 234.36,
          "end": 237.82,
          "en": "which is the default with Next.js 15 or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 237.82,
          "end": 240.42,
          "en": "higher, which is why you see multiple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 240.42,
          "end": 243.36,
          "en": "requests hitting the backend if you are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 243.36,
          "end": 247.18,
          "en": "using Next.js 15 or later because with no",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 247.18,
          "end": 251.28,
          "en": "store, Next.js will not store the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 251.28,
          "end": 252.78,
          "en": "yielded by the fetch request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 252.88,
          "end": 254.42,
          "en": "It will not cache it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 254.62,
          "end": 256.88,
          "en": "So you don't have that aggressive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 256.88,
          "end": 258.38,
          "en": "caching behavior there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 258.66,
          "end": 260.54,
          "en": "Of course, you could switch to force",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 260.54,
          "end": 263.2,
          "en": "cache if you wanted, if you want more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 263.2,
          "end": 267.04,
          "en": "efficiency, if you want more caching, but",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 267.04,
          "end": 270.56,
          "en": "the default with Next.js 15 is no store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 271.3,
          "end": 272.98,
          "en": "The other options, at least at the point of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 272.98,
          "end": 276.26,
          "en": "time where I'm recording this, are not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 276.26,
          "end": 278.5,
          "en": "important for the Next.js cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 278.5,
          "end": 278.98,
          "en": "management.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 279.8,
          "end": 283.92,
          "en": "But cache no store will tell Next.js that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 283.92,
          "end": 288.3,
          "en": "for this fetch request in this place, so not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 288.3,
          "end": 290.46,
          "en": "in other places where the same request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 290.46,
          "end": 293.5,
          "en": "is sent, but instead just in this place, the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 293.5,
          "end": 295.26,
          "en": "data should not be cached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 295.38,
          "end": 298.58,
          "en": "Instead, now with this setting, I'm",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 298.58,
          "end": 302.18,
          "en": "forcing Next.js to always send a new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 302.18,
          "end": 304.44,
          "en": "request and use the response data of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 304.44,
          "end": 306.86,
          "en": "that request instead of caching and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 306.86,
          "end": 307.84,
          "en": "reusing the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 309.28,
          "end": 311.54,
          "en": "And therefore, if I save that, I can already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 311.54,
          "end": 313.1,
          "en": "see that some new logs were added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 313.1,
          "end": 313.42,
          "en": "here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 313.96,
          "end": 316.34,
          "en": "The number may vary for you, but if I",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 316.34,
          "end": 317.96,
          "en": "reload the messages app a couple of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 317.96,
          "end": 320.5,
          "en": "times, you see more new log messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 320.5,
          "end": 321.08,
          "en": "were added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 321.42,
          "end": 324.28,
          "en": "So that's this no store setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 324.76,
          "end": 327.8,
          "en": "An alternative way of getting Next.js to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 327.8,
          "end": 331.22,
          "en": "revalidate the data is to again configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 331.22,
          "end": 333.54,
          "en": "the request, but now not with the cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 333.54,
          "end": 335.94,
          "en": "setting, but instead with the special next",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 335.94,
          "end": 339.56,
          "en": "setting, which is available on that fetch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 339.56,
          "end": 342.54,
          "en": "API if using it in a Next.js application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 342.86,
          "end": 345.44,
          "en": "because as I mentioned, Next.js extends",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 345.44,
          "end": 348.02,
          "en": "that fetch function and adds some new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 348.02,
          "end": 349.38,
          "en": "settings to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 349.54,
          "end": 351.44,
          "en": "For example, the next setting, which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 351.44,
          "end": 354.32,
          "en": "wants an object, which allows me to set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 354.32,
          "end": 355.7,
          "en": "a revalidate setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 357.02,
          "end": 360.58,
          "en": "And here I can define a number, which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 360.58,
          "end": 363.58,
          "en": "will be the number of seconds Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 363.58,
          "end": 366.44,
          "en": "should continue reusing the cache data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 366.44,
          "end": 369.14,
          "en": "until it will revalidate and throw away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 369.14,
          "end": 369.62,
          "en": "the cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
